      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Sherry Property Consultants are delighted to bring to the market this spacious six-bedroom detached dormer bungalow at Saint Martins, Jenkinstown, Dundalk, Co. Louth.\r\n\r\nBuilt in 1978 and extending to approximately 249 sq m (2,680 sq ft), the property occupies an elevated site of approximately 0.65 acres in a beautiful countryside setting. The elevated position enjoys fantastic views over Dundalk Bay and towards the Cooley Mountains, while large windows throughout the house make the most of the outlook and fill the property with an abundance of natural light.\r\n\r\nThe house has been beautifully decorated and is presented to a very high standard throughout. There is generous living accommodation along with six good-sized bedrooms, making this an ideal family home.\r\n\r\nOn the ground floor, the accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, sitting room, spacious living room, large kitchen, Utility room, WC, shower room and Bedroom 1. Upstairs, there are five further bedrooms, a generous family bathroom and additional WC.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property is approached through large stone walls with attractive stone piers and gated entrance. A large tarmac driveway provides extensive parking, while the generous lawn surrounds the house. The property also benefits from a large detached garage, providing excellent additional storage or workshop space.\r\n\r\nThis is an impressive and spacious family home, offering generous accommodation, excellent presentation, substantial grounds and a private, elevated setting. With its combination of space, character and convenient location, this property represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial family home in a highly desirable rural setting.\r\n\r\nLocation:\r\nThe property enjoys a peaceful countryside setting while benefiting from excellent connectivity to the surrounding towns and amenities. The area offers a wealth of local amenities and recreational opportunities, from scenic walks and mountain trails to nearby GAA facilities, primary and secondary schools. Carlingford is approximately 10 minutes away and Dundalk approximately 15 minutes, while Newry City is also within easy reach. The property is conveniently positioned for the M1 motorway, providing easy access north towards Newry and Belfast and south towards Drogheda and Dublin. This location offers an ideal balance of countryside living, accessibility and convenience, with the amenities of Dundalk, Carlingford and the wider North East all within easy reach."
      },
